Package: kerf
Title: Plan Spatial Batches for Raster and Vector Processing
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Michael D.", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2471-7511"))
Description: Describe how to split raster and vector data into batches
    for parallel or pipelined processing. A plan is a plain data frame
    with one row per batch, giving the members the batch owns (a raster
    window, an extent, a feature range or a predicate) and, optionally, a
    larger read-only context such as a halo of cells. Plans are made from
    metadata only, are checked against a column contract, and are read
    by any backend, so they suit dynamic branching in 'targets' and
    windowed reads with 'terra' or 'gdalraster'.
License: GPL-3
